    a: limbs[2],\n                b: limbs[3],\n            },\n        })\n    }","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Sample a QM31 challenge by per-limb rejection sampling (exactly"},{"DocComment":" uniform; soundness-note §3 T9)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Each limb draw takes 31 bits of a LE u32 and REJECTS the single"},{"DocComment":" non-canonical value P, redrawing from fresh transcript bytes: retries"},{"DocComment":" consume the next word of the block stream, and a spent block is"},{"DocComment":" replaced via `squeeze_block`, which advances the duplex state — no"},{"DocComment":" input is ever re-hashed, so retries cannot repeat a rejected value"},{"DocComment":" deterministically. The retry loop is bounded (`CHALLENGE_RETRY_LIMIT`)"},{"DocComment":" and exhaustion is an error the verifier surfaces as proof rejection:"},{"DocComment":" per-limb exhaustion probability is (2^-31)^8 = 2^-248, a completeness"},{"DocComment":" event (soundness-note §6), the correct trade on a CU-metered chain"},{"DocComment":" versus an unmetered loop."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In the non-rejecting case (all real transcripts, whp) this consumes"},{"DocComment":" exactly one block and produces the same limbs as the pre-fix sampler"},{"DocComment":" except on a P-hit, where the old code folded P to 0 (the ~2^-31"},{"DocComment":" per-limb bias this fix removes)."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":true,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":7720}],"output":{"Deduplicated":788}},"src":"TopLevel","is_global_initializer":null,"body":{"Structured":{"span":{"data":{"file_id":1,"beg":{"line":378,"col":4},"end":{"line":416,"col":5}},"generated_from_span":null},"b